#! interp=diagnostic jit=trap
# The interpreter raises a RUNTIME error (exit 1, rendered diagnostic);
# the JIT routes every runtime error through the single cx_trap channel
# (exit 126). Both reject; the shapes differ by design, so the pair is
# recorded and asserted rather than accepted as merely "non-zero".
D2.5c: reading .val on a dropped Handle must reject cleanly on both backends (interp: RuntimeError::StaleHandle; JIT: Trap/cx_trap, exit 126) -- neither is a panic.
